---
import AboutHeroImage from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Firmware engineer, software builder, and lifelong learner based in San Jose, California."
	pubDate={new Date('August 30 2026')}
	heroImage={AboutHeroImage}
>
	<h1><strong>Hi, I'm Adarsh!</strong></h1>

	<p>
		I'm a firmware engineer, software builder, and lifelong learner based in San Jose, California.
	</p>

	<p>
		By day, I work as a Silicon Firmware Development Engineer at Intel. I hold an MS in Electrical
		and Computer Engineering from Georgia Tech, and I love getting into the weeds of embedded systems.
		My technical interests span low-level microcontroller programming (C, C++, Rust, FreeRTOS) all
		the way to machine learning, computer vision, and robotics (PyTorch, ROS 2, Mujoco).
	</p>

	<p>
		Outside of my day job, I'm usually building something new. Whether it's developing a macro-tracking
		mobile app like KnapSnack, coding a retro web game, or deploying full-stack data visualization
		dashboards, I enjoy bringing ideas to life from the ground up. You can catch some of my ongoing side
		projects on Instagram at @adarsh.builds.
	</p>

	<p>
		When I'm not writing code or working on hardware, I'm dialing in my morning pour-over coffee routine,
		strength training, or reading up on economics and decision-making. On the weekends, I love taking my
		car out to explore California's coastal drives, hiking trails, and stargazing spots.
	</p>
</Layout>
